WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.108 --> 00:00:01.760
- According to the Nielsen
Total Audience Report,

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.316
in quarter one of 2017,

00:00:03.316 --> 00:00:04.786
the average American adult spent

00:00:04.786 --> 00:00:07.011
about 11 hours and 18 minutes a day

00:00:07.011 --> 00:00:08.698
consuming media content.

00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:09.632
This got me thinking.

00:00:09.632 --> 00:00:11.306
If we didn't have such easy access

00:00:11.306 --> 00:00:12.639
to unlimited entertainment,

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:13.970
what would we spend our time on--

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:14.803
Oh, I burped!

00:00:14.803 --> 00:00:16.405
What would we spend our time on?

00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:17.765
Hobbies? Laundry?

00:00:17.765 --> 00:00:19.347
Building an indestructible empire?

00:00:19.347 --> 00:00:20.407
To answer this question,

00:00:20.407 --> 00:00:23.153
I have persuaded three of my
all-too-trusting co-workers

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.795
to take the plunge and
stop streaming for a week.

00:00:25.795 --> 00:00:28.378
(mellow music)

00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:32.804
- There's not a day I'd go
without watching Netflix.

00:00:32.804 --> 00:00:34.813
I watch it when I get ready.

00:00:34.813 --> 00:00:37.439
Immediately when I get
home or when I'm cooking.

00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:39.801
Like, in the background for white noise.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.271
Now that I'm talking about it,

00:00:41.271 --> 00:00:43.401
I realize that I may have a problem.

00:00:43.401 --> 00:00:44.795
- I literally stream things

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:47.157
every second I'm on my bed or on my couch.

00:00:47.157 --> 00:00:49.132
I'll drop by my house and watch.

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:51.088
I'll stream something for lunch.

00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:53.375
- [Sara] Wait. You go
home and stream things?

00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:54.208
- Yeah.

00:00:54.208 --> 00:00:56.536
- I definitely watch once a day,

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:57.533
if not twice.

00:00:57.533 --> 00:00:59.687
Sometimes I let myself watch it

00:00:59.687 --> 00:01:01.185
while I put my makeup on in the mornings,

00:01:01.185 --> 00:01:02.182
but that's a treat.

00:01:02.182 --> 00:01:03.463
- Murder documentaries.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.325
- The OA.

00:01:04.325 --> 00:01:05.645
Love Game of Thrones.

00:01:05.645 --> 00:01:06.913
Love Broad City.

00:01:06.913 --> 00:01:07.811
- Sex and the City.

00:01:07.811 --> 00:01:08.702
This is Us.

00:01:08.702 --> 00:01:09.755
- Girls on HBO.

00:01:09.755 --> 00:01:10.784
Insecure.

00:01:10.784 --> 00:01:13.735
- Right now I'm addicted
to Vampire Diaries again.

00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:14.568
Why?

00:01:14.568 --> 00:01:15.651
I don't know.

00:01:16.758 --> 00:01:18.743
- So, I really wanna
deep clean my apartment,

00:01:18.743 --> 00:01:20.029
but I keep getting distracted.

00:01:20.029 --> 00:01:21.267
Reading is the biggest thing for me

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.007
because I have a bookshelf of books

00:01:23.007 --> 00:01:25.016
that I have read like five pages of each.

00:01:25.016 --> 00:01:28.161
- [Sara] So, you said you really
liked The Handmaid's Tale.

00:01:28.161 --> 00:01:29.293
- Yes. Oh, my god!

00:01:29.293 --> 00:01:31.405
- So, I got you some other
books by Margaret Atwood.

00:01:31.405 --> 00:01:32.809
- Oh, amazing!

00:01:32.809 --> 00:01:34.892
- And you also said
you wanted to organize.

00:01:34.892 --> 00:01:35.764
- I do.

00:01:35.764 --> 00:01:37.488
- So, I got you a drawer organizer.

00:01:37.488 --> 00:01:39.684
- Oh, that's so cute!

00:01:39.684 --> 00:01:41.918
- I've always wanted to learn how to cook.

00:01:41.918 --> 00:01:43.720
Everyone around me
knows that I can't cook.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.499
Also, my boyfriend loves boardgames.

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:49.095
If I had a choice between
boardgames or streaming,

00:01:49.095 --> 00:01:50.617
I'd rather watch something.

00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:53.140
This might encourage us
to play more boardgames.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.575
- So, I got you a Game
of Thrones cookbook.

00:01:55.575 --> 00:01:57.562
- Ah, this is so nice.

00:01:57.562 --> 00:02:00.356
- And then, I also got you a boardgame.

00:02:00.356 --> 00:02:01.904
- This feels nicer than streaming.

00:02:01.904 --> 00:02:03.176
I'm getting presents.

00:02:03.176 --> 00:02:04.733
- I think one of the things I would do

00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:06.552
is definitely work out more

00:02:06.552 --> 00:02:08.250
because I have gym in my apartment

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:11.397
and I haven't even been in it to see it.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.392
- [Sara] Okay, so first I have a book,

00:02:13.392 --> 00:02:14.857
'cuz you said you love the ocean

00:02:14.857 --> 00:02:17.411
and this seemed like a really good book.

00:02:17.411 --> 00:02:18.941
You did say you wanna exercise more,

00:02:18.941 --> 00:02:21.469
so I got you a kit to exercise at home.

00:02:21.469 --> 00:02:23.362
- Although I do have
a gym at my apartment,

00:02:23.362 --> 00:02:26.616
I am shy to go workout in front of people.

00:02:26.616 --> 00:02:27.687
So, cool.

00:02:27.687 --> 00:02:30.270
(mellow music)

00:02:32.292 --> 00:02:33.125
No.

00:02:34.815 --> 00:02:35.762
- That's a great idea.

00:02:35.762 --> 00:02:36.741
- Ah!

00:02:36.741 --> 00:02:37.845
- I'm excited now.

00:02:37.845 --> 00:02:40.297
(dramatic boom)

00:02:40.297 --> 00:02:41.768
Just informed my sister I'm doing this

00:02:41.768 --> 00:02:42.807
no-streaming thing

00:02:42.807 --> 00:02:45.561
and she wanted to watch
English TV while we eat

00:02:45.561 --> 00:02:47.036
and she's not too pleased.

00:02:47.036 --> 00:02:48.330
- (beep) stupid.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.055
- Life outside of Netflix--

00:02:50.055 --> 00:02:52.367
Real life is hard, okay?

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:55.347
Not only do I have to fill
this up half way today

00:02:55.347 --> 00:02:56.606
with the foot pump,

00:02:56.606 --> 00:02:59.601
I have to wait 24 hours
to continue to fill it up.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:00.880
- I'm standing in front of my TV.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.784
I just got home

00:03:01.784 --> 00:03:04.540
and I'm gonna unplug my Chromecast,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.098
which helps me stream things

00:03:07.098 --> 00:03:09.896
from my computer and phone.

00:03:09.896 --> 00:03:12.063
Unplugging the Chromecast.

00:03:17.514 --> 00:03:19.435
- My boyfriend really wanted to watch TV,

00:03:19.435 --> 00:03:22.199
so he is while I'm not facing it

00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:23.987
and facing the window.

00:03:23.987 --> 00:03:26.174
Literally just sitting here.

00:03:26.174 --> 00:03:28.960
(dramatic music)

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.841
- So, Maya told me that
she streamed an episode

00:03:31.841 --> 00:03:35.308
of the Vampire Diaries last night

00:03:35.308 --> 00:03:39.041
and that's against the rules, I'm afraid.

00:03:39.041 --> 00:03:40.275
- Oh, no.

00:03:40.275 --> 00:03:41.108
- How dare--

00:03:41.108 --> 00:03:42.876
How could you?

00:03:42.876 --> 00:03:44.876
- Before I started this,

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.437
I was watching the last
episode before the end

00:03:49.437 --> 00:03:52.161
of the entire series and I couldn't stop.

00:03:52.161 --> 00:03:53.233
- You couldn't wait?

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.912
So, I do have to tell you a
spoiler from Jane the Virgin.

00:03:55.912 --> 00:03:57.787
- Okay.
- In season three,

00:03:57.787 --> 00:04:00.454
episode ten from Jane the Virgin

00:04:02.165 --> 00:04:03.618
(beep)

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:04.451
- What?

00:04:05.862 --> 00:04:07.197
Wait.

00:04:07.197 --> 00:04:08.805
I'm gonna cry.

00:04:08.805 --> 00:04:09.996
But I'm done with Netflix.

00:04:09.996 --> 00:04:11.740
I've learned my lesson.
- You learned your lesson?

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.797
- That was the most, like, ugh!

00:04:14.797 --> 00:04:17.649
- And I also found out that Kane

00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:19.218
watched Game of Thrones.

00:04:19.218 --> 00:04:22.056
To be fair, it was the Game
of Thrones season premiere.

00:04:22.056 --> 00:04:26.286
So, maybe I was a little
harsh in expecting him

00:04:26.286 --> 00:04:27.984
to not watch that.

00:04:27.984 --> 00:04:29.231
Well, well, well.

00:04:29.231 --> 00:04:31.385
Look what we have here.

00:04:31.385 --> 00:04:33.259
- I did so well and then--

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:34.229
- [Sara] Did you do well?

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:35.386
I don't know.

00:04:35.386 --> 00:04:37.563
- I experienced life on a new level

00:04:37.563 --> 00:04:39.571
and then, Game of Thrones came out

00:04:39.571 --> 00:04:42.532
and I was just having so much FOMO.

00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:43.938
- [Sara] We're gonna
give you a spoiler from

00:04:43.938 --> 00:04:45.605
How to Get Away with Murder.

00:04:45.605 --> 00:04:46.572
I have not seen this show,

00:04:46.572 --> 00:04:48.706
so this means nothing to mean.

00:04:48.706 --> 00:04:50.629
There's a character
named Wes on this show.

00:04:50.629 --> 00:04:51.575
- Uh huh.

00:04:51.575 --> 00:04:53.822
- Apparently (beep)

00:04:53.822 --> 00:04:55.405
- No, you're lying!

00:04:57.970 --> 00:04:58.833
- [Sara] That was it.

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:00.500
- That was very sad.

00:05:02.545 --> 00:05:04.918
- So, I've just worked
out like a crazy person

00:05:04.918 --> 00:05:06.938
at this insane bootcamp thing

00:05:06.938 --> 00:05:08.269
and usually I'd come home

00:05:08.269 --> 00:05:11.420
and just be like chill
and watch TV and I can't,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.170
so I'm doing a puzzle

00:05:14.405 --> 00:05:16.566
like an 80 year old.

00:05:16.566 --> 00:05:19.199
- [Maya] Look at her go.

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:22.413
I filled it up and it came
with this little thing.

00:05:22.413 --> 00:05:26.022
But, I think we're gonna
use this in the pool.

00:05:26.022 --> 00:05:28.208
All right, we're about to
work out with this thing.

00:05:28.208 --> 00:05:30.007
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

00:05:30.007 --> 00:05:32.969
- It's a weekday and instead
of streaming something

00:05:32.969 --> 00:05:36.469
we're gonna play Game of Thrones Monopoly.

00:05:37.425 --> 00:05:38.258
- Look at this.

00:05:38.258 --> 00:05:39.953
The TV is not on.

00:05:39.953 --> 00:05:43.022
And I am gonna read this book

00:05:43.022 --> 00:05:46.442
like a grown up who doesn't
need TV to entertain them.

00:05:46.442 --> 00:05:47.504
Last night was the first time

00:05:47.504 --> 00:05:49.572
I actually decided to read

00:05:49.572 --> 00:05:51.768
for the last 20 minutes of me being awake

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:55.219
and I had forgotten how
calming reading actually is.

00:05:55.219 --> 00:05:57.187
It was like a really nice time.

00:05:57.187 --> 00:05:58.020
- Cheers.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.654
- Cheers.

00:05:59.654 --> 00:06:02.697
- All I wanna do is lay
in bed and watch Netflix.

00:06:02.697 --> 00:06:05.280
Hello, darkness. My old friend.

00:06:07.984 --> 00:06:09.736
- So, I've had a super long day

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.004
and I'm so exhausted

00:06:11.004 --> 00:06:14.362
and I just wanna lay down and watch TV

00:06:14.362 --> 00:06:17.411
and I'm wondering if DVDs count.

00:06:17.411 --> 00:06:21.417
- We actually went and got
pillows for the apartment.

00:06:21.417 --> 00:06:23.871
We went to a live comedy show at UCB.

00:06:23.871 --> 00:06:25.650
It was nice to explore the city

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.093
and not stay in our apartment.

00:06:27.093 --> 00:06:30.154
- Today is the last day of
not being able to stream

00:06:30.154 --> 00:06:31.712
and I'm so excited

00:06:31.712 --> 00:06:35.795
and I'm excited to watch
Netflix whenever I want.

00:06:36.772 --> 00:06:39.062
- Not streaming for a
week was really great.

00:06:39.062 --> 00:06:41.930
- I'm pretty happy to be done
with not streaming, honestly.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.677
- I hate when I get told
I can't do something

00:06:44.677 --> 00:06:46.465
'cuz then I wanna do it even more.

00:06:46.465 --> 00:06:48.132
- I definitely felt like a better person

00:06:48.132 --> 00:06:49.431
for not streaming all the time

00:06:49.431 --> 00:06:51.642
'cuz I do feel like a lazy
asshole when I do that.

00:06:51.642 --> 00:06:54.204
- I played a lot of boardgames.

00:06:54.204 --> 00:06:55.383
I cooked a lot.

00:06:55.383 --> 00:06:57.609
We finally furnished our apartment.

00:06:57.609 --> 00:06:59.835
I was a lot more
productive during the week.

00:06:59.835 --> 00:07:01.973
- I tried to set up that exercise ball,

00:07:01.973 --> 00:07:04.056
but it was so difficult

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.988
and I tried to read,

00:07:05.988 --> 00:07:08.092
but it was so difficult to focus.

00:07:08.092 --> 00:07:10.317
- I did read one of the short stories

00:07:10.317 --> 00:07:11.534
and I started to read the second one,

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.051
but haven't got any further.

00:07:13.051 --> 00:07:14.311
- So, instead, I ended up singing

00:07:14.311 --> 00:07:16.559
with my ukulele like every single night

00:07:16.559 --> 00:07:19.873
and ended up posting stuff
on Instagram like I used to

00:07:19.873 --> 00:07:21.390
and it was great.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:22.829
It was great to do that again.

00:07:22.829 --> 00:07:24.129
It felt so good.

00:07:24.129 --> 00:07:26.241
- I definitely would want to continue this

00:07:26.241 --> 00:07:28.000
maybe like half the week no streaming.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:28.833
You know?

00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:31.419
- I definitely wanna
try and stream less now.

00:07:31.419 --> 00:07:33.187
I definitely feel like I can get more done

00:07:33.187 --> 00:07:35.309
and I don't need it as much.

00:07:35.309 --> 00:07:38.562
I think it's just being allowed to have it

00:07:38.562 --> 00:07:39.611
is what I need.

00:07:39.611 --> 00:07:41.636
- I would definitely do
a streaming purge again

00:07:41.636 --> 00:07:44.922
just because I did so much creatively

00:07:44.922 --> 00:07:48.042
that I haven't done within this past year

00:07:48.042 --> 00:07:50.976
and I think it's good to
do everything in moderation

00:07:50.976 --> 00:07:52.163
and to take breaks.

00:07:52.163 --> 00:07:53.989
- I cannot wait to get back to This is Us

00:07:53.989 --> 00:07:55.458
'cuz I was so in the middle of it

00:07:55.458 --> 00:07:56.849
and excited about that show

00:07:56.849 --> 00:07:58.152
and then I had to just cut it off.

00:07:58.152 --> 00:08:01.122
- So, can I watch Netflix now?

00:08:01.122 --> 00:08:02.205
- [Sara] I guess.

00:08:02.205 --> 00:08:03.418
- Is it safe to?

00:08:03.418 --> 00:08:04.327
- [Sara] Sure.

00:08:04.327 --> 00:08:06.834
- Cool, 'cuz I was about
to watch it on my phone.

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:09.417
(upbeat music)

